>      The default playground directory is specified in too places:
> include/config.h and the Makefile in the top level directory.
> You probably already figured that out during the initial build
> and install.
>
>      Trying to update things manually is likely to result in
> problems.  You should use ``make all'' followed by ``make update''
> (instead of ``make install'') to rebuild the whole program and
> put everything into the proper place(s).  If you're using the
> DLB configuration ("data librarian", which packs almost all the
> data files into one big file) then you really need to let `make'
> rebuild the data as well as the program because putting one new
> file into nethack's directory won't accomplish anything.  That's
> probably why you can't find the existing castle.lev file now;
> it isn't a separate file in the installed playground directory.
